####Introduction room:
1) Main learning: Basics of metasploit and what makes it an useful tool ( It supports all phases of penetration testing engagement).
2) New terminologies introduced : i)Vulnerabilities , exploits , payloads(to get desired results from exploits)
ii)Encoders (tries to protect exploits and payloads from antivirus), evasion (actually evades evades antivirus softwares)
3)Commands that were introduced and used by me :> msfconsole -(Terminal)Launches metasploit
> ls , clear (similar function like in linux)
> search[keyword] ##Very useful command
> use_[module] ##
> show options ##
> back - leaves context 
> set_[parametername_value] -(example : set rhosts ip_address of target machine or set rport portnumber
4)My understanding of the Metasploit workflow : 
Start Metasploit
     ↓
Search for relevant module
     ↓
Select module
     ↓
Check required options
     ↓
Configure target
     ↓
